			"hasTextLink": false,
			"locked": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"type": "text",
			"version": 40,
			"x": 66.07156170255564,
			"y": 823.1437747976387,
			"width": 658.3984375,
			"height": 325,
			"strokeColor": "#ffa657",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"text": "🔍 Key design decisions\n\n1. **Keyword-only args** — `run_pipeline(*, functions_definition_path, ...)` forces named arguments.\n   Prevents bugs from mixing up positional arguments (3 string paths could be swapped easily).\n\n2. **Model instantiation** — `Small_LLM_Model()` is created once, not per prompt.\n   Reuses the loaded model across all 11 prompts (avoids re-downloading/reloading).\n\n3. **OutputItem wrapping** — Each decoded call is wrapped in a Pydantic OutputItem before writing.\n   This guarantees the JSON output schema is always valid.\n\n4. **The `decode()` boundary** — The pipeline doesn't know how constrained decoding works.\n   It just calls `decode()`. The decoder module handles all complexity (trie, logits, regex).\n   This is separation of concerns: pipeline orchestrates, decoder decodes.\n\n5. **Return type** — `list[dict[str, Any]]` makes the CLI layer easy:\n   pipeline returns plain dicts, no Pydantic dependency needed in the CLI.\n\n6. **Imports** — All imports are explicit: from .decoder import decode, not just import decoder.\n   You know exactly what names come from where.",
			"fontSize": 13,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"id": "JprL6cZs",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"elementType": "text",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "🔍 Key design decisions\n\n1. **Keyword-only args** — `run_pipeline(*, functions_definition_path, ...)` forces named arguments.\n   Prevents bugs from mixing up positional arguments (3 string paths could be swapped easily).\n\n2. **Model instantiation** — `Small_LLM_Model()` is created once, not per prompt.\n   Reuses the loaded model across all 11 prompts (avoids re-downloading/reloading).\n\n3. **OutputItem wrapping** — Each decoded call is wrapped in a Pydantic OutputItem before writing.\n   This guarantees the JSON output schema is always valid.\n\n4. **The `decode()` boundary** — The pipeline doesn't know how constrained decoding works.\n   It just calls `decode()`. The decoder module handles all complexity (trie, logits, regex).\n   This is separation of concerns: pipeline orchestrates, decoder decodes.\n\n5. **Return type** — `list[dict[str, Any]]` makes the CLI layer easy:\n   pipeline returns plain dicts, no Pydantic dependency needed in the CLI.\n\n6. **Imports** — All imports are explicit: from .decoder import decode, not just import decoder.\n   You know exactly what names come from where.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"versionNonce": 1968324891,
			"index": "a8",
